title: MikroTik REST API: NAND bad blocks
agents: mikrotik_rest_api
catalog: hw/network/mikrotik
license: GPL
distribution: check_mk
description:
 Share of bad blocks of the NAND flash of a MikroTik device ({bad-blocks}
 of {/system/resource}, reported in percent).

 A small share of bad blocks is normal for NAND flash, often already from
 the factory, and is handled by the flash management. The service is WARN
 at 2% and CRIT at 5% by default, configurable with the rule {MikroTik
 REST API: NAND bad blocks}. Written sectors since reboot and in total are
 shown in the details as an indicator for flash wear.

 Special agent {MikroTik RouterOS (mikrotik-rest-api)} in Setup > Agents >
 Other integrations, module "RouterOS Info, CPU, memory, system disk,
 uptime".

 Added in mikrotik-rest-api 1.2.3 by Klaus Paulitsch.

perfdata:
 Bad blocks in percent.

inventory:
 One service if the device reports bad blocks (devices with NAND flash).
